=== Connection to Latin rectangles ===
  A k×n Latin rectangle has distinct symbols in each row and column.
  Binary distinct row/column matrices are a special case.
  Number of k×n Latin rectangles: L(k,n) = n! × (n-1)! / (n-k)! × ...

=== Answer is a sum of counts ===
  318313204 ≈ 3.25 × 10^8
  This is roughly the number of 4×4 binary matrices
  with distinct rows and columns (total: 2^16=65536 space)
  Or a sum over several matrix dimensions.
